<section id="practitioner-planning" class="mt-8">
<h2>Document space, repeated trials and human review: worked planning guides</h2>
<p>Source inspected 14 November 2026: <a href={`${pinned}${d.source}`}>frozen AIRH insight snapshot</a>. SHA-256 of that entire JSON file: {d.sourceSha256}. Selected records: contextWindows.latestBreakdown.below1M nemotron-3.5-lightning ({d.context.context} tokens), and priceSpread.all mistral-large-4-0 ({d.price.input} dollars per million input tokens, {d.price.output} per million output). The price source label is preserved as “{d.price.source}”; its import time is {d.price.checked}. Neither this label nor import time is a new provider verification.</p>
<p>These are selected historical catalogue records, not a survey, live vendor quotes or measured performance. No new dataset is admitted. Existing source-policy and rights ownership remain unchanged. Context capacities and accounting at a particular endpoint require separate official verification. Model-price claims mean recorded values only.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/blog/document-space-after-reserves/">Document space</a>: hypothetical allowance = recorded context − 12,000 fixed input − output reserve. Reserves 8,000, 32,000, 64,000 give 242,144, 218,144, 186,144. No supported maximum-output claim. Shared-capacity accounting is an explicit teaching assumption, not a verified endpoint contract. No document is tokenised or submitted.</li>
<li><a href="/blog/repeated-model-trial-budget/">Repeated trial</a>: calls = 80 cases × 4 placeholder candidates × repeats (1, 3, 5). Each call is assumed to use 2,000 input and 1,000 output tokens; rate-based cost/call = (2,000 × 0.70 + 1,000 × 2.10)/1,000,000 = 0.0035 dollars. Costs: 1.12, 3.36, 5.60 dollars. All four placeholders use the same frozen rate to isolate repetition, not actual candidate-specific billing.</li>
<li><a href="/blog/human-review-token-bill/">Human review</a>: same assumed token counts across 10,000 jobs give 14 input dollars plus 21 output dollars = 35. Reviewed jobs = 10,000 × share (0.05, 0.2, 1). Review hours = reviewed jobs × 2/60. Review valuation = unrounded hours × assumed 30 dollars/hour. Hours round to two decimals only for display. These shares are neither error rates nor measured review requirements; the hourly rate is neither a wage claim nor financial savings evidence.</li>
</ul>
<p>Method terms are defined for these proposals: case = input plus written pass rule; attempt = one execution; candidate = configured setup; paired = matched by case; held out = separate from development choices; review share = fraction sent to a person. Record-keeping, timing and evaluation procedures are editorial proposals with no measured effectiveness claimed. A word-to-token conversion is deliberately not assumed.</p>
